title: Däumig's Price
subtitle: The Independents' leaders want guarantees.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_unification = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and e20_cg_daumig_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.e20_cg_daumig_done = 1;
RG.congress.tally();
!}
frequency: 400
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= Däumig's Price

Ernst Däumig asks for a word in private. He is a former Foreign Legion sergeant turned socialist editor, and he brought most of the delegates in this hall into the International. He wants to be co-chair of the new party, so that the Independents know they have joined a union and not been conquered. Behind him, the USPD's union officials want a promise that nobody will be expelled for sitting on a union executive with social democrats.

[? if congress_ahead = 1 : We are ahead, with [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 : The [+ congress_leader_name +] are ahead, with [+ congress_leader_votes +]% of the hall. ?]

- @chair: Promise Däumig the co-chair.
- @unions: Promise the union officials their posts.
- @no: Promise nothing.

@chair
subtitle: Many newcomers will come over to our slate. Our own current gives up a seat.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_daumig_deal = 1;
RG.congress.sway(0.08);
Q[Q.congress_backing + '_satisfaction'] -= 3;
Q.uspd_relation += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Däumig goes back to his delegates. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] of them vote with us from now on. ?] Our slate has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@unions
subtitle: The Saxon and Thuringian delegates will come over. The Left will say we have bought reformists.
on-arrival: {!
var n = RG.congress.convert('saxony', 0.25) + RG.congress.convert('berlin', 0.1) + RG.congress.convert('thuringia', 0.2);
RG.congress.tally();
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The officials get it in writing. Our slate has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@no
subtitle: Some of the newcomers will not take it well.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.bitter(5);
RG.congress.lose(0.03);
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.uspd_relation -= 4;
!}

Däumig is told that posts are for the congress to decide. He goes back to his delegates without a word. Our slate has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.
